! mcp_bootstrap_p120.strap -- the PRIME/UNPRIME error exits and the
! prime-queue control words, printed page 120.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.127, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID EA000149
!  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  120", and the header's own
! "LOCATION 215634" names the page's first word.
!
! FIFTEEN LINES AND NOTHING ELSE.  The page prints lines 1-15 and
! then stops; the rest of the sheet is blank.  Counted off the card
! serial column, which runs EA000149..EA000161 -- THIRTEEN cards for
! fifteen lines, because TWO CARDS EACH CARRY TWO STATEMENTS:
!   line 1 and line 2 are both EA000149  ("SIC,S DISIC ; B,S DISP")
!   line 8 and line 9 are both EA000155  (the same pair again)
! That is STRAP's semicolon, and C22-6728's prose prints the idiom
! in exactly this form -- "(SIC,STIC; B,SIFAD)".  The deck writes
! the two halves on two lines, which assembles identically; the
! card fact is recorded here and nowhere else.
!
! WHERE IT SITS.  printed p.119 line 50 is "M IF AS LVI,$14,S IF AS"
! at 215634.00, a half word, so the counter arrives here at
! 215634.40 and line 1 is the first row to spend it.  The trail is
! contiguous.  p.119 is not transcribed yet, so this deck sets its
! own origin with SLC,(8)215634.40 rather than inheriting one.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here, and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that
! printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Every name
! this page DEFINES is M-prefixed (M CR, M C 1, M PRM QK, M PRM ER,
! M P Q R, M R 4, M R 5, M MK 3, M PRIM Q, M MAXOP) and none of
! them collides with anything in pp.2-98.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Two error exits and the control words of the prime queue.
!
! Lines 1-2    the tail of an error exit that BEGINS ON p.119:
!              p.119 line 50 loads error code S IF AS into $14 and
!              these two lines store the IC and branch to the
!              dispatcher.  SIC,S DISIC saves the instruction
!              counter in the "LOCATION GENERATING ERROR CODE"
!              cell (that is S DISIC's own comment where it is
!              defined, 217451.40 "S DISIC VF,0"), then B,S DISP.
! Line 3   M CR     XW,S IPL IN  -CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS.
!                                An index word whose value field is
!                                the IPL tentacle table, S IPL IN,
!                                at 215016.00 (printed p.103 line
!                                53 defines it).  Count and refill
!                                are zero.
! Line 4   M C 1    DD(BU,24),2  a 24-bit constant 2, referenced
!                                from printed p.117 as "V+,$3,M C 1
!                                -ADD. 2 FOR NEXT PARAM."
! Line 5            CNOP         rounds 215637.30 up to a full word
!                                by planting a NOP half word.
! Line 6   M PRM QK DRZ(BU,64),(1)
! Line 7   M PRM ER LVI,$14,S PQ FUL  -- the SECOND error exit, and
!                                the one that starts on this page:
!                                load error code 79 "PRIME QUE TOO
!                                SMALL" and fall into
! Lines 8-9         SIC,S DISIC / B,S DISP, the same pair as 1-2.
!                                printed p.119 line 14 branches here
!                                ("BXHZ,M PRM ER -PRIME Q FULL").
! Line 10  M P Q R  XW,MPRIMQ,30,MPQR  -- the prime queue's control
!                                word: value = the queue M PRIM Q at
!                                215647.00, count = 30 (0o36), and
!                                refill = ITSELF, word 215643, so
!                                the queue reloads its own control
!                                word when it runs out.
! Lines 11-12 M R 4 / M R 5   one word each, the saved prime and
!                                unprime control words (printed
!                                p.119: "SX,$3,M R 4 -SAVE PRIME
!                                CONTROL", "SX,$3,M R 5 -REFILL
!                                UNPRIME CONTROL").
! Line 13  M MK 3   INDMK,.21,.55(.63)21  -- an indicator mask; see
!                                the note on the parenthetical entry
!                                mode below.
! Line 14  M PRIM Q DRZ(BU,32),(30)  -- the prime queue itself,
!                                thirty half words = fifteen words,
!                                215647.00..215666.00.
! Line 15  M MAXOP  SYN,SJC1    -MAX PP OP CODE.  A SYN, so it
!                                spends no storage and its printed
!                                LOCATION 000114.40+ is the resolved
!                                VALUE, not the counter.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE FIVE SYMBOLS THIS PAGE REFERENCES AND DOES NOT DEFINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! S IPL IN  215016.00  printed p.103 line 53 ("S IPL IN INDMK,4"),
!                      already in decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap as
!                      SIPLIN.  p.103's own header predicted this
!                      row.
! S DISIC   217451.40  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 289,
!                      SDISIC SYN,(8)217451.40.  Its defining card is
!                      OCR'd on PDF p.155 (printed p.148):
!                      "217451.40 000000.00+  S DISIC  VF,0
!                      -LOCATION GENERATING ERROR CODE".
! S PQ FUL  003411.00  SPQFUL, defined on printed p.107 line 33 as
!                      "SYN,(16)0709.0" and already landed in
!                      decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap.  0x709 = 1801
!                      = 0o3411.  THE SPELLING AND VALUE BOTH COME
!                      FROM THAT DECK, not from this page's ink.
! SJC1      000114.40  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p106.strap line 289,
!                      "SJC1 SYN, 76.32" (76*64+32 = 4896 bits =
!                      0o114.40).  Same: spelling taken from the
!                      landed deck.
! S DISP    217372.00  NEW HERE.  No landed deck defines it.  See
!                      the next note -- the printed "217372.10" is
!                      NOT its address.
!
! >>> S DISP IS 217372.00, NOT THE 217372.10 THE PAGE PRINTS. <<<
! Lines 2 and 9 print "217372.10 00" for "B,S DISP".  In a half
! word the printed octal pair is bits 18-23, and a branch's addr19
! occupies bits 0-18 -- so only the TOP bit of that pair belongs to
! the address and the other five are opcode.  0o10 = 001000 has its
! bit 18 CLEAR, so addr19 is even and the target is word 0o217372
! bit 0.  (Compare S DISIC on lines 1 and 8: "217451.40 80", 0o40 =
! 100000, bit 18 SET, which is why p.103 writes 217451.40 with the
! .40 and this one must not.)  Both spellings compile to the same
! thirty-two bits, so the !CHECK below cannot tell them apart -- the
! evidence that settles it is OCR'd PDF p.154 (printed p.147), which
! prints a full-word instruction NAMED "S DISP" at 217372.00.
! Twenty-one other rows in the OCR of this volume print "B,S DISP"
! with the identical half word; not one prints anything else.
!
! >>> ".55(.63)21" IS THE PARENTHETICAL INTEGER ENTRY MODE, AND IT
! IS NOT A TYPO FOR A LIST OF BITS. <<<  C28-6129 Section II printed
! p.25: "(.n)A" enters the unsigned integer A with its RIGHTMOST BIT
! at bit address .n, OR-ed into the field.  So line 13's second
! INDMK field is bit 55, then 21 decimal = 10101 laid down with its
! last bit at 63 -- bits 59, 61 and 63.  Five bits in all: 21, 55,
! 59, 61, 63, which is exactly the printed
! "000000.04 00  000000.01 15".  printed p.119 line 49 ("M MK 1
! INDMK,.53,.55(.63)21") prints "000000.05 15" in its second half
! for the same reason.  strap_asm already implements this
! (split_parenthetical_entries) and reproduces the word bit-exactly;
! nothing had to be added for this page.
!
! BARE DECIMAL BIT OFFSETS.  The INDMK fields are written ".21",
! ".55", ".63" with no "(8)", so they are DECIMAL -- and they must
! be, because bits 21, 55, 59, 61, 63 are what the page compiles.
! Written as octal they would land on 17, 45, 51.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION on lines 6, 11 and 14 -- "215640.00 *",
! "215644.00 *", "215647.00 *".  printed p.103 line 48 carries the
! same mark and p.37 line 29 and p.3 carry it too, and it was left
! unexplained there.  It does NOT simply mark a DRZ: line 12 is a
! DRZ(BU,64),(1) identical to line 11's and prints no star.  It
! changes no compiled bit and nothing here depends on it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS CHECKED, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY IS NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Eight of the fifteen rows carry a !CHECK.  The seven that do not:
!   lines 6, 11, 12, 14 are DRZ.  The "000001.00" / "000017.00" in
!     their BINARY OUTPUT column is the reservation's SIZE, not its
!     contents -- printed p.109's deck states the convention and
!     printed p.84 follows it.  0o17 = 15 words IS still read: it is
!     the (30) half words of line 14, and it is what puts the next
!     page's origin where it is.
!   line 15 is a SYN, which deposits no storage word; printed p.99's
!     convention, restated by p.102 and p.104, is !SYM only and never
!     a manufactured !CHECK.
!   lines 8 and 9 repeat lines 1 and 2 bit for bit and ARE checked.
! All ten defined symbols are checked against the LOCATION column.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! p.103 line 289; "SIC,S DISIC"
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.00            ! printed p.147 names it; see note
SIPLIN  SYN, (8)215016.00            ! printed p.103 line 53
SPQFUL  SYN, (16)0709.0              ! printed p.107 line 33, verbatim
SJC1    SYN, 76.32                   ! printed p.106 line 8, verbatim

        SLC, (8)215634.40

        SIC, SDISIC                  ! line  1  (card EA000149)
        B, SDISP                     ! line  2  (card EA000149)
MCR     XW, SIPLIN                   ! line  3  -CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS
MC1     DD(BU,24),2                  ! line  4
        CNOP                         ! line  5
MPRMQK  DRZ(BU,64),(1)               ! line  6
MPRMER  LVI, $14, SPQFUL             ! line  7
        SIC, SDISIC                  ! line  8  (card EA000155)
        B, SDISP                     ! line  9  (card EA000155)
MPQR    XW, MPRIMQ, 30, MPQR         ! line 10
MR4     DRZ(BU,64),(1)               ! line 11
MR5     DRZ(BU,64),(1)               ! line 12
MMK3    INDMK,.21,.55(.63)21         ! line 13
MPRIMQ  DRZ(BU,32),(30)              ! line 14
MMAXOP  SYN, SJC1                    ! line 15  -MAX PP OP CODE

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, read off PDF p.127 at 900 dpi
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!  LINE  LOCATION      BINARY OUTPUT                     NAME      STATEMENT                   COMMENT          CARD
!   1*   215634.40     217451.40 80                                SIC,S DISIC                                  EA000149
!   2*   215635.00     217372.10 00                                B,S DISP                                     EA000149
!   3*   215636.00     215016.00+ 000 000000 000000      M CR      XW,S IPL IN       -CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS  EA000150
!   4*   215637.00                          00000002     M C 1     DD(BU,24),2                                  EA000151
!   5*   215637.40     000000.30 00                                CNOP                                         EA000152
!   6*   215640.00 *   000001.00                         M PRM QK  DRZ(BU,64),(1)                               EA000153
!   7*   215641.00     003411.35 01                      M PRM ER  LVI,$14,S PQ FUL                             EA000154
!   8*   215641.40     217451.40 80                                SIC,S DISIC                                  EA000155
!   9*   215642.00     217372.10 00                                B,S DISP                                     EA000155
!  10*   215643.00     215647.00+ 000 000036 215643      M P Q R   XW,MPRIMQ,30,MPQR                            EA000156
!  11*   215644.00 *   000001.00                         M R 4     DRZ(BU,64),(1)                               EA000157
!  12*   215645.00     000001.00                         M R 5     DRZ(BU,64),(1)                               EA000158
!  13*   215646.00     000000.04 00   000000.01 15       M MK 3    INDMK,.21,.55(.63)21                         EA000159
!  14*   215647.00 *   000017.00                         M PRIM Q  DRZ(BU,32),(30)                              EA000160
!  15*   000114.40+    +00000000        NULL             M MAXOP   SYN,SJC1          -MAX PP OP CODE            EA000161

!SYM   MCR      215636.00
!SYM   MC1      215637.00
!SYM   MPRMQK   215640.00
!SYM   MPRMER   215641.00
!SYM   MPQR     215643.00
!SYM   MR4      215644.00
!SYM   MR5      215645.00
!SYM   MMK3     215646.00
!SYM   MPRIMQ   215647.00
!SYM   MMAXOP   000114.40

!CHECK 215634.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 1 SIC,S DISIC
!CHECK 215635.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 2 B,S DISP
!CHECK 215636.00 | 215016.00+ 000 000000 000000 | line 3 M CR XW,S IPL IN
!CHECK 215637.00 | 00000002 | line 4 M C 1 DD(BU,24),2 | 24
!CHECK 215637.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 5 CNOP
!CHECK 215641.00 | 003411.35 01 | line 7 M PRM ER LVI,$14,S PQ FUL
!CHECK 215641.40 | 217451.40 80 | line 8 SIC,S DISIC
!CHECK 215642.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 9 B,S DISP
!CHECK 215643.00 | 215647.00+ 000 000036 215643 | line 10 M P Q R XW,MPRIMQ,30,MPQR
!CHECK 215646.00 | 000000.04 00 000000.01 15 | line 13 M MK 3 INDMK,.21,.55(.63)21
